Fields that already hold the desired value are not written: a mixed update sends only the rest, and an update with nothing left reports no effect without a mutation; unrelated concurrent edits survive.
-- seed.json --
{"Issue": [{"id": "1a000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000123", "identifier": "ENG-123", "title": "Before title", "description": "Before body", "priority": 0}]}
-- run --
linear issue view ENG-123 --json > original.json
-- run --
linear issue update ENG-123 --unprotected --title "Already desired" --description "Unrelated edit" --json > concurrent.json
-- run --
linear issue update ENG-123 --title "Already desired" --priority 2 --base-file original.json --json
